	(text "Orient at right angle so digital\npins come out from the bottom"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 111.252 27.432 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "0e4c3c7f-f338-4ffb-b75f-b72d2bdf63bf")
	)
	(text "For the piezo driver channels, the load\n(28k resistor) sits on a different board.\nWe want the GND side of that resistor to sit\nat the same potential as the non-inverting\ninput to the PA95 op amp.\n\nSENSEN detects the IR drop from difference in\nground potentials (large power currents). Such\ncurrents do not flow through the SENSEN wire\nitself, thus IR drop is 0 across this one.\n\nSENSEP detects the small IR drop from up to 428 uA\ncurrent flowing through the OUT wire. Current across\nSENSEP is (OUT wire resistance / 40k) * 428 uA.\n\nIn the worst case, 5 inches of 28 AWG wire are 0.027 Ω.\nVoltage drop is up to 11 μV. That is 1 part in 2 million\nerror with 24 V range. With 15 mA (35x higher current),\nit is 1 part in 60,000 and noticeable.\n\nWe do not need to utilize SENSEP for this particular\nDAC, avoiding much confusion and debugging. Only a\ndifferential + and - pair for the voltage difference\nthat is transmitted between boards. OUT and SENSEN."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 22.606 19.304 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "5ab62847-c855-4285-8926-65ccc9e6c6da")
	)
